A default constructor is implicitly defined by Java if a constructor doesn't exist.
	The default constructor initializes the capacity field to an int's default value, 0.

Field initialization is usually preferred over using a constructor.
	However, sometimes initializations are more complicated, in which case a constructor is needed.

